"First, we need to find the total number of students in the school. We know that the ratio of female students to the total number of students is 4 to 9, and there are 396 female students. Let \\( T \\) be the total number of students. Then, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{396}{T} = \\frac{4}{9}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( T \\):\n\n\\[\nT = 396 \\times \\frac{9}{4} = 891\n\\]\n\nNext, we know the ratio of teachers to students is 1 to 11. Let \\( N \\) be the number of teachers. Then, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{N}{891} = \\frac{1}{11}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( N \\):\n\n\\[\nN = 891 \\times \\frac{1}{11} = 81\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of teachers is \\(\\boxed{81}\\)."
