"To find the greatest possible length of each piece, we need to determine the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the lengths of the two ropes. The lengths of the ropes are 18 meters and 24 meters.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorizations of the numbers:\n- \\(18 = 2 \\times 3^2\\)\n- \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3\\)\n\nThe GCD is found by taking the lowest power of each prime that appears in both factorizations:\n- The lowest power of \\(2\\) is \\(2^1\\).\n- The lowest power of \\(3\\) is \\(3^1\\).\n\nThus, the GCD is:\n\\[ \\text{GCD} = 2^1 \\times 3^1 = 2 \\times 3 = 6 \\]\n\nTherefore, the greatest possible length of each piece is \\(\\boxed{6}\\) meters."
